Feature: BL-975 BL-967's owed 30-minute live soak is run and its verdict recorded

  PARKED, PERMANENTLY NON-EXECUTABLE (specifier, 2026-08-22). This file is a
  `.feature.draft`: no `*.feature` glob and no acceptance runner picks it up,
  and no step handler is owed for it by anyone. It states the evidentiary bar
  QA judges the soak against, in the reviewable form Gherkin gives it — it is
  not, and will never be, a mechanically-run contract.

  Why it is parked rather than wired (QA finding 2, evidence f8e61157b):
  this chore changes no code. Its deliverable is a live wall-clock observation
  recorded as a QA judgment. The only "gate" an executable handler could apply
  is a grep of the evidence markdown for its own conclusions — which asserts
  that words were written, not that the observation happened or was read
  correctly. A handler that instead read the real logs would have to reach
  `.swarmforge/daemon/*.log`, a live runtime path acceptance handlers are
  forbidden to touch, and would rot the moment those logs rotate (which is the
  very thing that blocked this ticket). Either way there is no honest gate
  here, so this ticket carries none. The operative contract is the ticket's
  own `qa_e2e_procedure`, judged by QA and recorded in
  `backlog/evidence/BL-975-soak-<date>.md`.

  Background:
    Given the recorded soak evidence file for this ticket under "backlog/evidence/"

  # BL-975 bl967-owed-live-soak-recorded-01
  Scenario: the evidence pins the observation window to a confirmed post-fix daemon
    Then the evidence names the observed daemon's build sha and shows BL-967's fix commit is an ancestor of it
    And the evidence spans an observation window of at least 30 minutes inside that daemon's uptime
    And the evidence lists the handoffd freshness-incident entries inside that window, or states there were none

  # BL-975 bl967-owed-live-soak-recorded-02
  Scenario: the verdict is coherent with the observed delta
    Then a zero-incident window with completed heartbeat cycles records verdict PASS
    And a window containing any handoffd freshness incident or attributed in-cycle timeout records the attributed sweep and call and names the follow-on ticket minted for it
